        {
            "number": 4,
            "revision": "33fa4abb9df74a54e76ee78899e50aad8446c249",
            "parents": [
                "a93f3ea1a80a4d02983572f0ceb8b4692e2bd057"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/47/89247/4",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Ender",
                "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
            },
            "createdOn": 1776224335,
            "author": {
                "name": "Eric Liu",
                "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                "username": "liuer-sys"
            },
            "kind": "NO_CHANGE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Please don't wrap at 20 characters.\n\nPlease add a \"why\" here.  I don't know what a NetworkAdapter is compared to a NetworkInterface (which we already have) compared to a Board compared to a PCIeDevice.  Why do we need an explicit type for NetworkAdapter and how is it intended to be consumed by applications (other than entity-manager)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks!\nNetworkAdapter represents a physical network adapter\nhardware (e.g. Ethernet NICs, converged network\nadapters), mapping to the Redfish NetworkAdapter\nresource.\n\nbmcweb uses Item.NetworkAdapter as a D-Bus mapper\nfilter to expose the Redfish NetworkAdapter resource\ntree.\n\nExisting interfaces cannot substitute:\n- NetworkInterface is a logical network interface\n  (maps to Redfish EthernetInterface), not physical\n  network adapter hardware.\n- Board is too generic for bmcweb to distinguish\n  which objects are network adapters.\n- PCIeDevice describes PCIe identity \u2014 GPUs are also\n  PCIeDevice, so bmcweb cannot use it to distinguish\n  network adapters from other PCIe devices.\n\nThis interface follows the same pattern as\nFabricAdapter: an empty interface (no properties)\nwith a connecting association to Connector.Port.\n\nHow it is used:\n- dbus-sensors creates Item.NetworkAdapter on the\n  network adapter object and sets up a connecting\n  association to its Port objects.\n- bmcweb discovers all objects with\n  Item.NetworkAdapter via mapper query to expose\n  the Redfish NetworkAdapter collection, then follows\n  the connecting association to find Port objects.\n\nFull implementation:\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/q/topic:\"CX_NetworkDeviceFunctions\""
                }
            ],
