        {
            "number": 5,
            "revision": "048bef805a241ec12d543ca9643531016b94f84e",
            "parents": [
                "a93f3ea1a80a4d02983572f0ceb8b4692e2bd057"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/47/89247/5",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Eric Liu",
                "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                "username": "liuer-sys"
            },
            "createdOn": 1776318824,
            "author": {
                "name": "Eric Liu",
                "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                "username": "liuer-sys"
            },
            "kind": "NO_CODE_CHANGE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Did you consider renaming `Item.Ethernet` for this purpose\n\n```\ncat yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/Ethernet.interface.yaml \ndescription: >\n    Implement to provide Ethernet card attributes.\n```\n\nFrom a quick search it does not look like it's used much\n\nhttps://github.com/search?q=org%3Aopenbmc%20xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Item.Ethernet&type=code\n\nand its description is kind of similar to what's being proposed.\n\nIf you don't want to re-use/re-name it, should it be documented as deprecated? Or should one implement both interfaces?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for your help!\nLooking at Item.Ethernet, its description is \"Ethernet card attributes\", which seems to be scoped to Ethernet.\n\nNetwork adapters like the NVIDIA ConnectX series(ConnectX-7, ConnectX-8) support both Ethernet and InfiniBand protocol modes, so Item.Ethernet may not be the best fit. Item.NetworkAdapter represents physical network adapter hardware without being tied to a specific protocol, which seems more appropriate for this use case.\n\nIndeed, Item.NetworkAdapter semantically covers Item.Ethernet, so marking Item.Ethernet as deprecated would make sense. I'll follow whatever approach upstream prefers \u2014 please let me know how you'd like to handle this and I'll get it done.\nIf my understanding is incorrect, please feel free to correct me. Thanks!"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the detailed explanation \ud83d\ude0a\n\nI would be fine with adding a small note to `yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/Ethernet.interface.yaml`, something like:\n\n\"This interface is deprecated, use `xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Item.NetworkAdapter` instead.\"\n\nSince bmcweb only seems to use the `NetworkAdapter` interface anyways\n\n```\n[alexander@alexanderarchlinux bmcweb]$ rg -i \"Item.Ethernet\"\n[alexander@alexanderarchlinux bmcweb]$ rg -i \"Item.NetworkAdapter\"\nredfish-core/lib/network_adapter.hpp\n28:    \"xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Item.NetworkAdapter\"};\n```\n\nNot sure what @patrick@stwcx.xyz thinks is right here or what's the history on the `Item.Ethernet`."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "I've updated in PS6 \u2014 marked Item.Ethernet as deprecated and pointed to Item.NetworkAdapter (see lines 4-7):\n\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/+/89247/6/yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/Ethernet.interface.yaml#4\n\nIf the direction changes after further discussion, I will adjust accordingly.\n\nThanks for help!"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/NetworkAdapter.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 4,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Since it maps to Redfish NetworkAdapter resource, should we document that here?\n\nIt would clarify why anyone would create this interface beyond just modeling things on D-Bus."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/NetworkAdapter.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 4,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "I've updated in PS6\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/+/89247/6/yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/NetworkAdapter.interface.yaml#6\nThanks for advice."
                }
            ],
